WEBVTT

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.310
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Right, Thursday. Everyone awake, more or less?</v>

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:18.559
<v Jamie Brennan>More or less. Whose new car is that in the car park? The shiny one taking up about a space and a half.</v>

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.620
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one with more mud than paint.</v>

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.589
<v Jamie Brennan>Looks like it's only just come out of the showroom. Brave bringing it here.</v>

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:34.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Give it a week. It'll match the rest.</v>

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:38.320
<v Callum Reid>Right, car reviews later. Think we've got all eight of us.</v>

00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:44.329
<v Priya Raman>Can you hear me? Teams has picked the wrong microphone again.</v>

00:00:46.759 --> 00:00:50.609
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're coming through. Bit hollow, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:54.289
<v Priya Raman>That's probably just me, then.</v>

00:00:56.119 --> 00:01:00.320
<v Callum Reid>Ha. Marc, anything from last night before we get into the updates?</v>

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.299
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, finished the repair on the pop valve last night. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:07.819
<v David Whitfield>Ah, good stuff.</v>

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.519
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. Dave, where are you with yours?</v>

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:16.260
<v David Whitfield>The pressure-drop investigation, I've boxed that off. All done.</v>

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:19.430
<v Callum Reid>Good, thanks.</v>

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:26.989
<v David Whitfield>And I'm not chasing that purchase order now. The other shift already sorted it, so that chase is cancelled.</v>

00:01:28.209 --> 00:01:31.709
<v Jamie Brennan>Fair enough. No point two shifts doing the same chase.</v>

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:35.719
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Hannah, how about you?</v>

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:43.439
<v Hannah Price>Um, the near-miss write-up's blocked. Waiting on the permit to be signed, so I can't take it any further.</v>

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:45.609
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Frustrating, that.</v>

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:51.769
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. On my pressure-drop investigation, I've done the prep; just the write-up left.</v>

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.340
<v Callum Reid>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:04.560
<v Marcus Hale>Saz asked me to pass on the sensor recalibration on the line 1 mould temp. She's still on it, going fine so far.</v>

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marc. Wasn't sure I'd get on the call when we spoke.</v>

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.610
<v Sarah Okafor>And my purchase-order chase is done. All signed off.</v>

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:19.699
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. Right, today's new bits, then.</v>

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:27.150
<v Callum Reid>Hannah Price, can you swap the filter on the cooling tower at half two? No rush.</v>

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.000
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll swap it at half two.</v>

00:02:30.479 --> 00:02:32.580
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. It's not an urgent one.</v>

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.080
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's fine with me.</v>

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.400
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, I talked over the end there. Only said okay.</v>

00:02:41.229 --> 00:02:47.180
<v Callum Reid>No worries. I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by 11am. No rush on that either.</v>

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Cal. Happy with that.</v>

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:53.319
<v Callum Reid>Nothing elaborate, just a toolbox talk.</v>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.069
<v Jamie Brennan>So not forty slides and a motivational video?</v>

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.020
<v Callum Reid>You've ruined the surprise now.</v>

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:10.099
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, so I'll sort the training records for the new starters as well. No rush on those.</v>

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Marc.</v>

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:18.370
<v Marcus Hale>Honestly, feels like there's more paperwork to being new than actually being new.</v>

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:22.729
<v Hannah Price>You stop being new just as you learn where everything lives.</v>

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.770
<v Callum Reid>Sounds about right. Mide, you were about to come in?</v>

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:35.110
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. I'll go to the sub to pick up the replacement parts for the counterbalances after lunch.</v>

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:38.389
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Mide. Top priority please, that one.</v>

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:43.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Understood. I'll make that my top priority after lunch.</v>

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:47.979
<v Jamie Brennan>Actual parts collection, not your scenic tour past the coffee machine.</v>

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:52.819
<v Olumide Adeyemi>One time, Jamie. You've had about six months out of that.</v>

00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:57.159
<v Priya Raman>That's pretty good value for a coffee, to be fair.</v>

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:04.169
<v Callum Reid>Right, before this becomes a full review of everyone's breaks—any other new work to raise?</v>

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.520
<v David Whitfield>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.669
<v Priya Raman>No, nothing from electrical.</v>

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:12.110
<v Hannah Price>Nothing else here.</v>

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.430
<v Sarah Okafor>No more from me either. All clear on what's been agreed.</v>

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:19.529
<v Callum Reid>Okay, that's everyone, then.</v>

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Still reckon that car belongs to a visitor. Nobody here keeps anything that clean.</v>

00:04:26.129 --> 00:04:28.579
<v David Whitfield>Speak for yourself. I washed mine. Once.</v>

00:04:30.589 --> 00:04:34.089
<v Callum Reid>On that impressive note, we'll leave it there. Cheers, everyone.</v>
